# brave-browser: the Brave lion head. The silhouette is the mane, a narrow tuft on top,
# shoulders that jump wide two rows down and a chin that tapers to a point, traced from
# the shipped product_logo_256.png rather than invented.
#
# The white is the whole point of this logo and it is not a face full of detail, it is a
# big T. A brow band straight across, a 2px nose bridge running down the middle, two
# orange notches left and right of it as the eyes, and a separate white diamond at the
# bottom as the muzzle. On top of that the brow ends run three rows down the outer sides
# and step inward, which is what the original does and what Nikola asked for.
#
# Colour is a new extra.hex ramp, ff8a4c / fb4d0d / a32f0a. Brave is #ff4f01, and Endesga's
# f77622 is both yellower and the exact face colour of places/folder, so reusing it would
# have put two orange blocks next to each other in the panel.
#
# Rejected: a plain silhouette with no mask (reads as a shield, not a lion), masks derived
# automatically by thresholding the downscaled logo (asymmetric, read as a V), a two row
# brow (crushes the nose bridge at 16px), brow ends hanging outward (noisy at 16px), and
# white pulled all the way around the cheeks (turns into a white border, loses the face).
A ff8a4c
B fb4d0d
C ffffff
D a32f0a
